`q = 1, r = v1 - q*v2` (signed overflow, wraps) → `r = v1 - INT_MIN`; then `r>=0 ? q : q + 1` | ✅ `err_f3_v1neg_v2_intmin` |\n| 8 | `f3` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 >= 1` (guarded `-v1` overflow path, uses `-(v1+v2)`) | `q = -((-(v1+v2))/v2) - 1`, `r = -((-(v1+v2))%v2)` | ✅ `err_f3_v1_intmin_v2pos` |\n| 9 | `f3` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 < 0 && v2 != INT_MIN` (uses `-(v1-v2)`) | `q = ((-(v1-v2))/(-v2)) + 1`, `r = -((-(v1-v2))%(-v2))` | ✅ `err_f3_v1_intmin_v2neg` |\n| 10 | `f3` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 == INT_MIN` (final `else`) | `q = 1, r = 0` → returns `1` | ✅ `err_f3_both_intmin` |\n| 11 | `f3` | any input where the computed remainder `r < 0` | returns `q + (v2 > 0 ? -1 : 1)` (the floor correction) | ✅ `err_f3_negative_remainder` |\n| 12 | `f4` | `rnd == NULL` | **no null check** — `cn_rnd_next` dereferences → SIGSEGV (UB). Rust must be identically unchecked (documented, not executed) | ⚠️ documented, see `err_null_pointers_documented` |\n| 13 | `f4` | `state = {0, 0}` (degenerate xorshift seed) | `value = 0` → `result = 1023<<52` → returns exactly `0.0` | ✅ `err_f4_zero_state` |\n| 14 | `f4` | `state = {UINT64_MAX, UINT64_MAX}` (max seed) | pure integer path, no rejection; result in `[0,1)` | ✅ `err_f4_max_state` |\n| 15 | `f5` | any bit above bit 15 set (masks are 16-bit: `0xAAAA`, `0x5555`, …) | high bits are **silently discarded**; result always `< 0x10000` | ✅ `err_f5_high_bits_discarded` |\n| 16 | `f5` | `a == 0xFFFFFFFF` / `a == 0` | `0x0000FFFF` / `0` | ✅ `err_f5_extremes` |\n| 17 | `f7` | `channels == 2` (the `channels != 2` / `channels == 2` predicate switch) | first term becomes `0`, terms 2 and 3 activate | ✅ `err_f7_channels_two` |\n| 18 | `f7` | `bitdepth == 32` (the `bitdepth != 32` predicate) | `bitdepth + 0` instead of `bitdepth + 1` in term 3 | ✅ `err_f7_bitdepth_32` |\n| 19 | `f7` | `blocksize`/`channels`/`bitdepth` large enough to overflow `uint32_t` (e.g. `0xFFFFFFFF`) | **no range check** — unsigned wrap-around modulo 2³² | ✅ `err_f7_overflow_wrap` |\